= Hilbert's third problem - 1/28/2020

#statement("Definition")[
A $n$-#strong[simplex]#index-entry("Simplex") $Delta^n$ is the convex hull of $n + 1$ general positioned points $v_0\,dots.h.c\,v_(n + 1)$, called its #strong[vertices]#index-entry("Vertex"), a #strong[face]#index-entry("Face") is the convex hull of some vertices

]
#statement("Definition")[
A #strong[polytope]#index-entry("Polyhedron") $P$ is such that $P = Delta_1 union dots.h.c union Delta_m$, where $Delta_i$'s are simplices and the interiors of $Delta_i$ are disjoint, and $Delta_i inter Delta_j$ is precisely a common face

We say $P$ is a #strong[generalized polytope]#index-entry("Generalized polytope") if without the last condition

