#statement("Example")[
Tuple chain complex $C_(*)\(X\)$ in Definition #ref(label("Definition of tuple chain complex"), supplement: none) is a filtered chain complex with filtration #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r C_(*)^(p - 1)\(X\)arrow.r C_(*)^p\(X\)arrow.r C_(*)^(p + 1)\(X\)arrow.r dots.h.c arrow.r C_(*)\(X\)$) If $X$ is a topological space with a filtrations of subspaces(CW complex with skeletons is a special case) #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c subset.eq X^(p - 1) subset.eq X^p subset.eq X^(p + 1) subset.eq X$) Then the singular chain complex $C_(*)^(upright(s i n g))\(X\)$ is a filtered chain complex with filtration #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r C_(*)\(X^(p - 1)\)arrow.r C_(*)\(X^p\)arrow.r C_(*)\(X^(p + 1)\)arrow.r dots.h.c arrow.r C_(*)\(X\)$)

]
#statement("Definition")[
Suppose $R$ is a commutative ring with identity

A #strong[graded module]#index-entry("Graded module") is a module with grading $A = xor.big_n A_n$, $n in I$ is a totally ordered set, mostly we just consider $bb(Z)$

A #strong[filtered module]#index-entry("Filtered module") is a module with a filtration #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r.hook F_(p - 1) A arrow.r.hook F_p A arrow.r.hook F_(p + 1) A arrow.r.hook dots.h.c arrow.r.hook A$) We can define the graded module associated to the filtration $g r A = xor.big_p F_(p + 1) A\/F_p A$

A #strong[filtered graded module]#index-entry("Filtered graded module") is a graded module $A = xor.big_n A_n$ with a filtration of graded modules #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r.hook F_(p - 1) A arrow.r.hook F_p A arrow.r.hook F_(p + 1) A arrow.r.hook dots.h.c arrow.r.hook A$) Such that filtration preserving grading, i.e. $F_p A subset.eq xor.big_(n lt.eq p) A_n$, then we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $F_p A = F_p A inter.big xor.big_(n lt.eq p) A_n = xor.big_(n lt.eq p) F_p A inter A_n$) Define $\(F_p A\)_n$ or $F_p A_n := F_p A inter A_n$, then #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r.hook F_(p - 1) A_n arrow.r.hook F_p A_n arrow.r.hook F_(p + 1) A_n arrow.r.hook dots.h.c arrow.r.hook A_n$) Is a filtration of $A_n$, and $\(F_p A\)_n$ are the direct summands of $F_p A$, we also have a grid

