#statement("Example")[
Let $C_(*)$ be a filtered chain complex, the homology $H_(*) C = xor.big_p H_p C$ is a graded graded module with filtration with $F_p H_n C = upright(i m)\(H_n\(F_p C\)arrow.r H_(*) C\)$

]
#statement("Definition")[
A #strong[spectral sequence]#index-entry("Spectral sequence") is a sequence of bigraded module ${ E_(*\,*)^r }$ together with differentials $partial_(p\,q)^r : E_(p\,q)^r arrow.r E_(p - r\,q + r - 1)^r$ such that $partial^r compose partial^r = 0$ and $E^(r + 1) tilde.equiv ker partial^r\/upright(i m) partial^r = : Z^r\/B^r$, $E^r$ are called the $r$-th page

