Since $Z^(i + 1)\,B^(i + 1)$ are submodules of $Z^i\/B^i$, we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c subset.eq B^i subset.eq B^(i + 1) subset.eq dots.h.c subset.eq Z^(i + 1) subset.eq Z^i subset.eq dots.h.c$) Define $B^oo = union.big_r B^r$, $Z^oo = inter.big_r Z^r$, $E^oo = Z^oo\/B^oo$

]
#statement("Definition")[
A spectral sequence converges to a filtered graded module $A$ if $E_(p\,q)^oo = F_p A_(p + q)\/F_(p - 1) A_(p + q)$, or equivalently $xor.big_(p + q = n) E_(p\,q)^n = g r A_n$, we write as $E_(p\,q)^1 arrow.r.double A_(p + q)$

