#statement("Theorem", title: [Serre spectral sequence])[
Let $F arrow.r E arrow.r B$ be a filtration, suppose $pi_1\(B\)$ acts on $H_(*)\(F\)$ trivially, then there is a spectral sequence with $E_(p\,q)^2 = H_p\(B\;H_q\(F\)\)arrow.r.double H_(p + q)\(E\)$, meaning converges to $H_(*)\(E\)$

]
#statement("Example", title: [Wang sequence])[
Suppose $F arrow.r E arrow.r B$ be a filtration, with $B = S^k$, then $E_(p\,q)^2 = H_p\(B\;H_q\(F\)\)= H_p\(B\)times.o H_q\(F\)$ by universal coefficient theorem, since $H_p\(B\)= cases(delim: "{", bb(Z)\, & p = 0\,k, 0\, & upright("Otherwise"))$, we have the second page

