#statement("Theorem")[
Suppose $C_(*)$ is filtered chain complex, then there is a spectral sequence $E_(p\,q)^1 = H_(p + q)\(F_p C\/F_(p - 1) C\)arrow.r.double H_(p + q)\(C\)$ with differential $partial^1 : H_(p + q)\(F_p C\/F_(p - 1) C\)arrow.r H_(p + q - 1)\(F_(p - 1) C\/F_(p - 2) C\)$ induced by the composition of boundary map and quotient map $H_(p + q)\(F_p C\/F_(p - 1) C\)arrow.r H_(p + q - 1)\(F_(p - 1) C\)arrow.r H_(p + q - 1)\(F_(p - 1) C\/F_(p - 2) C\)$

]
#statement("Remark")[
Suppose the filtration is in the first quadrant, we can view $Z_(p\,q)^r$ as #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, ${c in F_p C_(p + q) mid(bar.v) partial c in F_(p - r) C_(p + q - 1)} + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$) $B_(p\,q)^r$ as #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $partial F_(p + r - 1) C_(p + q + 1) + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$) $E_(p\,q)^r$ as #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $frac({c in F_p C_(p + q) mid(bar.v) partial c in F_(p - r) C_(p + q - 1)} + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q), partial F_(p + r - 1) C_(p + q + 1) + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q))$) Then $Z_(p\,q)^0 = F_p C_(p\,q)$, $B_(p\,q)^0 = F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$, $E_(p\,q)^0 = F_p C_(p + q)\/F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$, $E_(p\,q)^1 = H_(p + q)\(F_p C_(*)\/F_(p - 1) C_(*)\)$

$Z_(p\,q)^oo = {c in F_p C_(p + q) mid(bar.v) partial c = 0} + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$, $B_(p\,q)^oo = partial C_(p + q + 1) + F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)$, $E_(p\,q)^oo = frac(Z_(p + q)\(F_p C_(*)\)+ F_(p - 1) C_(p + q), B_(p + q)\(C_(*)\)+ F_(p - 1) C_(p + q)) = frac(F_p H_(p + q)\(C\), F_(p - 1) H_(p + q)\(C\)) = frac(upright(i m)\(H_(p + q)\(F_p C\)arrow.r H_(p + q)\(C\)\), upright(i m)\(H_(p + q)\(F_(p - 1) C\)arrow.r H_(p + q)\(C\)\))$

]
#statement("Example")[
Let $X$ be a CW complex, consider $C_(*) = C_(*)^(upright(s i n g))\(X\)$, $F_p C_(*) = C_(*)^(upright(s i n g))\(X^p\)$, $E_(p\,q)^1 = H_(p + q)\(X^p\,X^(p - 1)\)= cases(delim: "{", C_p^(upright(c e l l))\(X\)\, & q = 0, 0\, & upright("Otherwise"))$, $partial^1$ is just the cellular boundary map, thus $E_(p\,0)^2 = E_(p\,0)^oo = H_p^(upright(c e l l))\(X\)tilde.equiv H_p^(upright(s i n g))\(X\)$

]
#statement("Example")[
Suppose $A subset.eq X$ is a subspace, consider $0 subset.eq C_(*)\(A\)subset.eq C_(*)\(X\)$, $E_(1\,q)^1 = H_(q + 1)\(X\,A\)$, $E_(0\,q)^1 = H_q\(A\)$ with $partial^1 : H_(q + 1)\(X\,A\)arrow.r H_q\(A\)$ induced by the boundary map, then we have exact sequences #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r E_(1\,q)^oo arrow.r H_(q + 1)\(X\,A\)arrow.r H_q\(A\)arrow.r E_(0\,q)^oo arrow.r 0$) #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r E_(0\,n)^oo arrow.r H_n\(X\)arrow.r E_(1\,n - 1)^oo arrow.r 0$) Which give us the long exact sequence for $\(X\,A\)$

]
#statement("Definition")[
A #strong[double complex]#index-entry("Double complex") $C_(*\,*)$ is $bb(Z)$-bigraded with two differentials $partial' : C_(p\,q) arrow.r C_(p - 1\,q)$, $partial' : C_(p\,q) arrow.r C_(p\,q - 1)$ such that $\(partial'\)^2 =\(partial''\)^2 = 0$ and $partial' partial'' + partial'' partial' = 0$\($partial'\,partial''$ anticommutes)

Define the #strong[total chain complex]#index-entry("Total chain complex") $T o t_n := xor.big_(p + q = n) C_(p\,q)$, $partial = partial' + partial''$

]
#statement("Example")[
Suppose $C_(*)\,D_(*)$ are chain complexes, $C_(*) times.o D_(*)$ is defined to be the total complex of the double complex $C_(p\,q) := C_p times.o D_q$, $partial' := partial^C times.o 1$, $partial'' :=\(- 1\)^p 1 times.o partial^D$

]

