#statement("Theorem", title: [Algebraic Künneth formula])[
If $C_(*)\,D_(*)$ are chain complexes, then we have an exact sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r xor.big_(p + q = n) H_p\(C\)times.o H_q\(D\)arrow.r H_n\(C times.o D\)arrow.r xor.big_(p + q = n - 1) T o r\(H_p\(C\)\,H_q\(D\)arrow.r 0$)

]#label("Algebraic Kunneth formula")
#statement("Theorem", title: [Topological Künneth formula])[
Since $C_(*)\(X times Y\)tilde.equiv C_(*)\(X\)times.o C_(*)\(Y\)$, apply Theorem #ref(label("Algebraic Kunneth formula"), supplement: none), we get an exact sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r xor.big_(p + q = n) H_p\(X\)times.o H_q\(Y\)arrow.r H_n\(X times Y\)arrow.r xor.big_(p + q = n - 1) T o r\(H_p\(X\)\,H_q\(Y\)arrow.r 0$)

]
#statement("Example")[
Consider $C_(p\,q) := C_q^(upright(s i n g))\(overbrace(X times dots.h.c times X, p)\)$, $partial' := sum\(- 1\)^i epsilon_i$, where $epsilon_i : C_q^(upright(s i n g))\(X^p\)arrow.r C_q^(upright(s i n g))\(X^(p - 1)\)$ by removing the $i$-th coordinate, $partial'' :=\(- 1\)^p partial$

]
#statement("Definition")[
Suppose $C_(*\,*)$ is a double complex, there are two natural filtrations on $T o t_(*)$, $' F_p T o t_n = xor.big_(r lt.eq p) C_(r\,n - r)$, $'' F_p T o t_n = xor.big_(r gt.eq p) C_(n - r\,r)$, hence we have two corresponding spectral sequences

For $' F_p T o t_(*)$, $' E_(p\,q)^1 = H_(p + q)\(' F_p T o t_(*)\/' F_(p - 1) T o t_(*)\)= H_q\(C_(p\,*)\)$, $partial^1 = partial'$, $' E_(p\,q)^2 = H_p\(H_q\(C_(p\,*)\)\)$

For $'' F_p T o t_(*)$, $'' E_(p\,q)^1 = H_(p + q)\(' F_p T o t_(*)\/'' F_(p - 1) T o t_(*)\)= H_p\(C_(*\,q)\)$, $partial^1 = partial''$, $'' E_(p\,q)^2 = H_p\(H_q\(C_(p\,*)\)\)$

However, unlike $partial'$ has bidegree $\(- 1\,0\)$ which matches up with that $partial^1$ normally has bidegree $\(- 1\,0\)$, $partial''$ has bidegree $\(0\,- 1\)$, there are two ways to work around this

\(1) Flip the double complex $C'_(p\,q) = C_(q\,p)$

\(2) Flip the differential

]

