= Cohomological spectral sequence - 2/20/2020

#statement("Definition")[
A #strong[cohomology spectral sequence]#index-entry("Cohomology spectral sequence") is a bigraded module ${ E_r^(p\,q) }$ with differentials $d_r^(p\,q) : E_r^(p\,q) arrow.r E_r^(p + r\,q - r + 1)$ such that $d_r compose d_r = 0$

Suppose $A^(*)$ is a filtered graded module with a descending filtration #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $A supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq F^(p + 1) A^(*) supset.eq F^p A^(*) supset.eq F^(p - 1) A^(*) supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq dots.h.c$) We say $E_1^(p\,q) arrow.r.double A^(*)$ if $E_oo^(p\,q) = frac(F^p A^(p + q), F^(p + 1) A^(p + q))$

]
#statement("Remark")[
The convergence also preserves cup product

]
#statement("Theorem", title: [Serre's cohomology spectral sequence])[
Suppose $F arrow.r E arrow.r B$ is a fibration, $pi_1\(B\)$ acts on $H_(*)\(F\)$ trivially, then we have a cohomology spectral sequence with $E_r^(p\,q) = H^p\(B\;H^q\(F\)\)arrow.r.double H^(p + q)\(E\)$

]#label("Serre's cohomology spectral sequence")
#statement("Example")[
$H^(*)\(S U\(n\)\)= and.big_(bb(Z))\[x_3\,x_5\,dots.h.c\,x_(2 n - 1)\]$, where $x_i in H^i\(S U\(n\)\)$, $and.big_R\[a_1\,dots.h.c\,a_n\]$ is the exterior algebra generated by $a_1\,dots.h.c\,a_n$

]
#proof(title: "Proof")[
Use induction, we already knew $H^(*)\(S U\(1\)\)= H^(*)\(p t\)= bb(Z)$ with trivial multiplication, $H^(*)\(S U\(2\)\)= H^(*)\(S^3\)= and.big_(bb(Z))\[x_3\]$, now suppose we know $H^(*)\(S U\(n - 1\)\)= and.big_(bb(Z))\[x_3\,x_5\,dots.h.c\,x_(2 n - 3)\]$

Consider fibration $S U\(n - 1\)arrow.r S U\(n\)arrow.r S^(2 n - 1)$, $U mapsto U e_1$, apply Theorem #ref(label("Serre's cohomology spectral sequence"), supplement: none), $E_2^(p\,q) = H^p\(S^(2 n - 1)\,H^q\(S U\(n - 1\)\)\)tilde.equiv H o m_(bb(Z))\(H^p\(S^(2 n - 1)\)\,H^q\(S U\(n - 1\)\)\)$, we can show $E_2 = E_oo$, thus $H^q\(S U\(n\)\)= E_2^(0\,q) xor E_2^(2 n - 1\,q - 2 n + 1) = H^q\(S U\(n - 1\)\)xor H^(q - 2 n + 1)\(S U\(n - 1\)\)$

]

