#statement("Example")[
Suppose $dots.h.c subset.eq F_(p - 1) C_bullet subset.eq F_p C_bullet subset.eq dots.h.c$ is a filteration of chain complex $C_bullet$, exact sequence $0 arrow.r F_(p - 1) C_bullet arrow.r F_p C_bullet arrow.r\(g r C_bullet\)_p arrow.r 0$ give a long exact sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r H_n\(F_(p - 1) C_bullet\)arrow.r^(i_(*)) H_n\(F_p C_bullet\)arrow.r^(j_(*)) H_n\(F_p C_bullet\/F_(p - 1) C_bullet\)arrow.r^(k_(*)) H_(n - 1)\(F_(p - 1) C_bullet\)arrow.r dots.h.c$) If we write $D_(p\,q)^1 := H_(p + q)\(F_p C_bullet\)$, $E_(p q)^1 := H_(p + q)\(F_p C_bullet\/F_(p - 1) C_bullet\)$, then the long exact sequence become #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $dots.h.c arrow.r D_(p\,q)^1 arrow.r D_(p + 1\,q - 1)^1 arrow.r E_(p\,q)^1 arrow.r D_(p\,q - 1)^1 arrow.r dots.h.c$) Consider $D^1 = xor.big D_(p\,q)^1$, $E^1 = xor.big E_(p\,q)^1$, then $\(D^1\,E^1\,i_(*)\,j_(*)\,k_(*)\)$ form an exact couple, note that $d_r : E_(p\,q)^r arrow.r E_(p - r\,q + r - 1)^r$

]
#statement("Lemma")[
Suppose $dim X = n$, we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $F_p C_k\(X\)\/F_(p - 1) C_k\(X\)= cases(delim: "{", 0\, & p < k upright(" or ") p > n, xor.big_U F_p\(C_k\(U\)\/F_(p - 1) C_k\(U\)\, & upright("otherwise"))$) Where $U lt.eq X$ runs over $p$ dimensional planes

]
#statement("Lemma")[
Suppose $dim X = p$, $H_(p + q)\(C_(*)\(X\)\/F_(p - 1) C_(*)\(X\)\)= 0$ for any $q > 0$

]
#statement("Theorem")[
Consider spectral sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $E_(p\,q)^1 = xor.big_U H_(p + q)\(C_(*)\(U\)\/F_(p - 1) C_(*)\(U\)\)= cases(delim: "{", xor.big_U cal(P)\(U\,1\)\, & q = 0, 0\, & q > 0)$) Since $E^r$ converges to $H_(*)\(X\)$, if $X = bb(R)^n\,bb(H)^n$, we have exact sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r xor.big_(dim U = n) cal(P)\(U\,1\)arrow.r dots.h.c arrow.r xor.big_(dim U = 0) cal(P)\(U\,1\)arrow.r^epsilon bb(Z) arrow.r 0$) If $X = S^n$, we have exact sequence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $0 arrow.r bb(Z) arrow.r xor.big_(dim U = n) cal(P)\(U\,1\)arrow.r dots.h.c arrow.r xor.big_(dim U = 0) cal(P)\(U\,1\)arrow.r bb(Z) arrow.r 0$) Here the maps can be thought of as take $k$ dimensional polygons on the $k$ dimensional faces

]

