= Group homology - 3/5/2020

#statement("Theorem")[
$K\(-\,n\)$ is a functor from of the category of groups to the category of topological spaces or to the category of CW complexes. $K\(-\,n\)$ respects product, i.e. $K\(G times H\,n\)= K\(G\,n\)times K\(H\,n\)$ since $pi_n\(product X_i\)= product_i pi_n\(X_i\)$

]
#statement("Lemma")[
$G$ is a group, there exists a contractible space $X$ on which $G$ acts freely

]#label("Existence of EG")
#proof(title: "Proof")[

]
#statement("Theorem")[
$G$ is a group, $H_i\(G\)tilde.equiv H_i\(K\(G\,1\)\)$

]
#proof(title: "Proof")[
