#proof(title: "Proof")[
Define double complex #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $A_(p\,q) = xor.big_(bb(R)^n ⊋ U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) tilde(C)_q\(U_p\)_(T\(U_p\)) = cases(delim: "{", bb(Z) & \,p = q = - 1, C_q\(bb(R)^n\)_T & \,p = - 1\,q gt.eq 0, xor.big_(U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) bb(Z) & \,p gt.eq 0\,q = - 1, xor.big_(U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) C_q\(U_p\)_(T\(U_p\)) & \,p\,q gt.eq 0, )$) $partial' = sum\(- 1\)^i epsilon_i$, $partial'' =\(- 1\)^p partial$. As additive groups $U_p tilde.equiv T\(U_p\)$, hence #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $' E_(p\,q)^1 = cases(delim: "{", xor.big_(U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) H_q\(tilde(C)_(*)\(U_p\)_(U_p)\)= xor.big_(U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) H_q\(U_p\)= xor.big_(U_0 supset.eq dots.h.c supset.eq U_p) and.big_(bb(Z))^(*) U_p & \,p gt.eq 0, H_q\(tilde(C)_(*)\(bb(R)^n\)_T\)= H_q\(bb(R)^n\)= and.big_(bb(Z))^(*) bb(R)^n & \,p = - 1)$) This is complex $C_(*)\(F\,and.big^q\)$

Claim: higher differentials of $' E$ is zero

For any $a in bb(Z)$, consider $mu_a : bb(R)^n arrow.r bb(R)^n$, $x mapsto a x$ which induces multiplication by $a^q$ on $and.big_(bb(Z))^q U arrow.r and.big_(bb(Z))^q U$, $A_(p\,q) arrow.r A_(p\,q)$, since $mu_a$ commutes with differentials $partial^r : E_(p\,q)^r arrow.r E_(p - r\,q + r - 1)^r$, we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $a^q partial^r x = partial^r mu_a x = mu_a partial^r x = a^(q + r - 1) partial^r x arrow.r.double r = 1 upright(" or ") partial^r x = 0$) Hence $' E_(p\,q)^2 =' E_(p\,q)^oo = H_p\(F\,and.big^q\)$. Since $U lt.eq bb(R)^n$ is a $bb(Q)$ vector space, $and.big_(bb(Z))^(*) U = and.big_(bb(Q))^(*) U$ is also a $bb(Q)$ vector space, $H_k\(T o t\(A\)\)$ has a $bb(Q)$ vector space filtration $0 subset.eq F_(- 1) subset.eq dots.h.c subset.eq F_(k - 1) = H_k\(T o t\(A\)\)$, $H_k\(T o t\(A\)\)= E_(- 1\,k)^oo xor dots.h.c xor E_(k - 1\,2)^oo$ is the eigenspace decomposition

#math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $'' E_(p\,q)^1 = cases(delim: "{", 0 & \,q gt.eq 0, C_(*)\(bb(R)^n\)\/F_(n - 1) C_(*)\(bb(R)^n\) & \,p = - 1)$) #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $'' E_(- 1\,q)^oo ='' E_(- 1\,q)^2 = H_q\(C_(*)\(bb(R)^n\)\/F_(n - 1) C_(*)\(bb(R)^n\)\)$) Hence $cal(P)\(bb(R)^n\,T\)='' E_(- 1\,n)^2 = H_(n - 1)\(T o t\(A\)\)$ is a $bb(Q)$ vector space

]
