$U = {mat(delim: "(", 1, b; 0, 1) mid(bar.v) b in F} tilde.equiv F$ is the unipotent subgroup. Use Hochshild-Serre spectral sequence #ref(label("Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence"), supplement: none) we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $H_p\(F^times\;and.big_(bb(Q))^q\(F\)\)= H_p\(F^times\;H_q\(F\;bb(Z)\)\)= H_p\(B\/U\;H_q\(U\;bb(Z)\)\)arrow.r.double H_(p + q)\(B\;bb(Z)\)$) For any $r in F$, consider #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $mu_r : and.big_(bb(Q))^q\(F\)arrow.r and.big_(bb(Q))^q\(F\)\,thin x_1 and dots.h.c and x_q mapsto\(r x_1\)and dots.h.c and\(r x_q\)= r^q\(x_1 and dots.h.c and x_q\)$) Apply Center kills lemma #ref(label("Center kills lemma"), supplement: none), $\(r^q - 1\)$ annihilates $H_q\(F^times\;and.big_(bb(Q))^q\(F\)\)$, hence $H_q\(F^times\;and.big_(bb(Q))^q\(F\)\)= 0$ for $q > 0$, therefore inclusion $T arrow.r.hook B$ and projection $B arrow.r T$ induce isomorphisms #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $H_(*)\(F^times\;bb(Z)\)tilde.equiv H_(*)\(B\;bb(Z)\)$) Note that $mu_F tilde.equiv bb(Q)\/bb(Z)$ is the torsion subgroup of $F^times$, by Proposition #ref(label("Homology of abelian groups"), supplement: none), we get #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $H_(*)\(G\;C_0\)= H_(*)\(G\;C_1\)= H_(*)\(F^times\;bb(Z)\)= and.big_(bb(Q))^(*)\(F^times\/mu_F\)xor.big H_(*)\(mu_F\;bb(Z)\)$) Since $T o r$ preserves direct sums and filtered colimits, or through some Bockstein, we have #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $H_(*)\(mu_F\;bb(Z)\) & = T o r_(*)^(bb(Z)\[mu_F\])\(bb(Z)\,bb(Z)\)\
 & = T o r_(*)^(bb(Z)\[mu_F\]) (xor.big_p bb(Z) \[ 1 / p \] \/ bb(Z) \; bb(Z))\
 & = T o r_(*)^(bb(Z)\[mu_F\]) (xor.big_p lim_arrow.r_n bb(Z) \/ p^n bb(Z) \; bb(Z))\
 & = xor.big_p T o r_(*)^(bb(Z)\[mu_F\]) (lim_arrow.r_n bb(Z) \/ p^n bb(Z) \; bb(Z))\
 & = xor.big_p lim_arrow.r_n T o r_(*)^(bb(Z)\[mu_F\]) (bb(Z) \/ p^n bb(Z) \; bb(Z))\
 & = cases(delim: "{", xor.big_p lim_arrow.r_n bb(Z) = xor.big_p bb(Z) & i = 0, xor.big_p lim_arrow.r_n bb(Z)\/p^n bb(Z) = mu_F & i upright(" odd"), 0 & i > 0 upright(" even"))$) Here $bb(Z)\[1 / p\]\/bb(Z) = lim_arrow.r_n bb(Z)\/p^n bb(Z)$ is the Prüfer group

By Lemma #ref(label("Hyperhomology of an acyclic chain complex is the same as homology"), supplement: none) and Theorem #ref(label("Hyperhomology spectral sequence"), supplement: none) we know #math.equation(block: true, numbering: none, $E_(p q)^1 = H_q\(G\;C_p\)= H_q\(C_p times.o_(bb(Z)\[G\]) B_(*)\(G\)\)arrow.r.double bb(H)_(p + q)\(G\;C_(*)\)= H_(p + q)\(G\;bb(Z)\)$) Hence the $E^1$ page looks like

